# Git commit messages

Every commit subject must start with one of these prefixes. Do not invent others.

| Prefix | Use for |
| --- | --- |
| `feat:` | New feature |
| `fix:` | Bug fix |
| `refactor:` | Code refactoring |
| `docs:` | Documentation |
| `style:` | Formatting, missing semicolons, etc. |
| `test:` | Adding tests |
| `chore:` | Maintenance |

Subject after the prefix: concise, imperative, lowercase. Keep the existing commit protocol: HEREDOC, no `--no-verify`, only commit when asked.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Start the subject with exactly one allowed prefix
- Write the rest in imperative mood (`add`, `handle`, `document`)

**Don't**

- Omit the prefix
- Use `wip:`, `update:`, `changes:`, or any prefix not in the table
- Capitalize the subject after the prefix (`feat: Added the garden list page`)

```
feat: add garden list page
fix: handle missing garden id
docs: document commit message prefixes
```

```
Add garden list
wip: stuff
feat: Added the garden list page
```
